{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And they commanded Joseph, etc.</b> One needs to know the reason for his saying <b>lemor</b> (to say), for if the intention was to say to Joseph, it should have said ״לֵאמֹר אֶל יוֹסֵף״ (to say to Joseph). Perhaps what was intended is that the speaker should not tell him that the brothers sent him concerning this matter, but rather should say that he heard from their father commanding the brothers to say these things to him. And this is why he said a second time <b>lemor</b> (to say). Understand this:"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:51:20.695857239Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}